  "name": "Building Blocks - Common Workflow Language building blocks",
  "abstract": "Common Workflow Language (CWL) is an open standard for describing how to run command line tools and connect them to create workflows.\n",
  "description": "Tools and workflows described using CWL are portable across a variety of platforms that support the CWL standards. \nUsing CWL, it is easy to scale complex data analysis and machine learning workflows from a single\ndeveloper's laptop up to massively parallel cluster, cloud and high performance computing environments.\n\nMore information at [the Common Workflow Language website](https://www.commonwl.org/).\n",
  "sparqlEndpoint": "https://defs-dev.opengis.net/fuseki/query",
  "modified": "2026-09-07T11:25:26.777680",
  "tooling": {
    "bblocks-postprocess": {
      "commitId": "\"865a527f37dc271186cb8dd7d0386365bf1486d3",
